1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,832
On a typical day, about two thirds of Earth is covered by clouds.

2
00:00:03,832 --> 00:00:05,928
What if they all vanished for a week?

3
00:00:06,417 --> 00:00:07,937
First, the rain stops.

4
00:00:07,937 --> 00:00:12,291
A typical puffy cloud holds about five hundred tonnes of water.

5
00:00:12,291 --> 00:00:14,296
No clouds, no rain, anywhere.

6
00:00:14,783 --> 00:00:15,758
Days get hotter.

7
00:00:15,758 --> 00:00:18,012
Clouds bounce sunlight back to space.

8
00:00:18,012 --> 00:00:22,520
Overall, they cool the planet by about twenty watts on every square meter.

9
00:00:23,017 --> 00:00:24,386
But nights get colder.

10
00:00:24,386 --> 00:00:26,066
Clouds work like a blanket.

11
00:00:26,066 --> 00:00:27,932
Under clear, dry desert skies,

12
00:00:27,932 --> 00:00:32,786
the temperature can drop about twenty degrees Celsius from afternoon to night.

13
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,758
Solar panels would love it.

14
00:00:34,758 --> 00:00:35,687
Farmers wouldn't.

15
00:00:35,687 --> 00:00:38,581
By the end of the week, you'd really miss a gray day.

16
00:00:39,083 --> 00:00:41,702
What if Earth lost its magnetic shield instead?

17
00:00:41,702 --> 00:00:43,151
Full story on the channel.
